{title: Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{artist: Henry van Dyke / Ludwig van Beethoven}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{key_original: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 64장}
{title_ko: 기뻐하며 경배하세}
{score: joyful-joyful.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Joyful, joyful, we a[A]dore Thee
[D]God of glory, [A]Lord of [D]love
[D]Hearts unfold like [A]flowers before Thee
[D]Opening to the [A]sun a[D]bove
[Bm]Melt the clouds of [F#m]sin and sadness
[G]Drive the dark of [D]doubt away
[D]Giver of im[A7]mortal gladness
[D]Fill us with the [A7]light of [D]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]All Thy works with [A]joy surround Thee
[D]Earth and heaven re[A]flect Thy [D]rays
[D]Stars and angels [A]sing around Thee
[D]Center of un[A]broken [D]praise
[Bm]Field and forest, [F#m]vale and mountain
[G]Flowery meadow, [D]flashing sea
[D]Singing bird and [A7]flowing fountain
[D]Call us to re[A7]joice in [D]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Thou art giving [A]and forgiving
[D]Ever blessing, [A]ever [D]blessed
[D]Wellspring of the [A]joy of living
[D]Ocean depth of [A]happy [D]rest
[Bm]Thou our Father, [F#m]Christ our Brother
[G]All who live in [D]love are Thine
[D]Teach us how to [A7]love each other
[D]Lift us to the [A7]joy di[D]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Mortals, join the [A]mighty chorus
[D]Which the morning [A]stars be[D]gan
[D]Father love is [A]reigning o'er us
[D]Brother love binds [A]man to [D]man
[Bm]Ever singing, [F#m]march we onward
[G]Victors in the [D]midst of strife
[D]Joyful music [A7]leads us sunward
[D]In the triumph [A7]song of [D]life
{end_of_verse}
